  reading behind D198, D199, D201–D204, D206 and D358.

**What (a) leaves, by date only** (no hit has been read):
- v34-3m read up to 08-28;
- the split-v3 trial and the v117 smoke read 08-29 and 08-30.
- So the scored span can only be **08-31 to 09-20**: three weeks of 218, 229 and 273 articles (720), less whatever the census finds (D613
  already found 10 in the week of 09-07 and 4 in the week of 09-14).

**The amendment:**
- Plan §1.3 item 1 samples 40 kept articles a week. Over three weeks that is about 120 articles. The fresh week's reading (40 articles)
  gave 8 matters, 5 listed by both families. Across weeks many matters recur and merge, so N may fall below 20 by sampling alone.
- **Proposed:** read **every** kept article in the scored span instead of 40 a week. Same brief (A1), same two families, same merge and
  reconciliation, in batches of about 40 articles per session.
- Decided now: no hit has been read, the census has not started, and no system has run.
- The rest of the plan is unchanged. The systems still run from empty at 07-01, so the warm-up is now 07-01 to 08-30, and the cutoff stays
  09-20.

**Questions:**
1. Is this amendment faithful to D665 and D667? D665: "scored on unread weeks from 07-20 up to 09-20, as far as the full exposure census
   supports". Does it move any finish line after outputs are seen?
2. Anything else (a) changes in the plan that must be fixed before the census starts?

