    22	**Choice (a).** D667 makes the absence of a cited tuning case a condition for exempting the whole folder. Reading (b) would preserve more dates, but an article can shape a change through a sample or an aggregate finding without being named. The folder-level reading gives D665’s claim of unread weeks the firmer basis.     1	# My own classification, written before reading either reader's answer
     2	
     3	**Leaning: reading (b), article level.** My confidence is moderate, and the council decides.
     4	
     5	## Why (b)
     6	
     7	- **The purpose.** D667 states it: "a replay of the product as it ran tunes neither system". Exposure is a property of an article: was its
     8	  content used to shape either system or the readers?
     9	- **v29-3m.** D199 rewrote the extraction rule from an aggregate count over the run: 493 empty answers in 1,553 calls, 65% of the first
    10	  week's items. That is a census of a behaviour, not the content of the scored-week articles.
    11	- **v34-3m.**
    12	  - D205 doubled an output cap after one judgement hit it. That is generic.
    13	  - D206's writer change came from a judgement's duplicate id.
    14	  - The served-copy edit removed v68's rows from data, not from either system.
    15	- **Later freezes.** The old extraction prompt was later rebuilt and frozen (v74i) on golden-v5, which covers 07-01 to 07-14. The new system
    16	  never read these runs as input.
    17	
    18	## The risk Codex named
    19	
    20	An article can inform tuning without being named. Under (b), that risk is held by three things:
    21	- every research artifact built from these runs is a read, including the 2026-10-28 quality review and any trace census document that
    22	  quotes articles;
    23	- every decision's quoted passages count;
    24	- the full census reads documents, not only run folders.
    25	
    26	## What each reading leaves, by date only
    27	
    28	| | (a) Folder level | (b) Article level |
    29	|---|---|---|
    30	| v29-3m and v34-3m | reads | exempt |
    31	| First possible scored day | about 08-29 (v34 ran to 08-28) | 07-20 |
    32	| Scored weeks | about 3: 08-31, 09-07 and 09-14 (the split-v3 trial also read 08-29 and 08-30) | 07-20 to 09-20 |
    33	| Articles left | about 700 | about 1,619, less the dev arms' `items-window` reads (about 527 by the earlier reviewer's count, if all are reads), the research reads, and D613's 14 |
    34	| N | at 40 articles a week, about 120 articles are read, and N may fall below 20 | — |
    35	
    36	## Classification
    37	
    38	- **Every configuration trial, arm, week test and day smoke** listed in the brief: read.
    39	- **The run3 family:** production use at the time (D63: sealed, window to 08-15). Its in-span reads are all in `items-window`, which the dev
    40	  arms also read, so the class does not change the outcome. Exempt.
    41	- **v29-3m:** exempt under (b), read under (a).
